    "body": "By LoadstarEditorial\n22 November 2026\nhttps://youtu.be/3fSyWnjcFzM\nAs the Gemini alliance prepares for a full return to Suez transits, could greater stability finally bring improved schedule reliability? And with ocean freight rates cooling on some trades, why are containership charter rates continuing to climb?\nThe Loadstar’s managing editor Gavin van Marle joins us to unpack the latest developments in ocean shipping, from mounting costs for India-Gulf shippers to carrier earnings and shifting freight rates.\nThen, CHAMP Cargosystems’ Anna Klekner explores the fallout from the FAA’s nationwide ground stop, the risks of growing digital dependence and the progress of IATA’s ONE Record initiative. Plus, with transpacific airfreight rates reaching new highs, we examine how airlines are adapting their pricing strategies.\nClick here to receive an email notification every time we release a podcast.\nThis article is © The Loadstar. Reproduction, rewriting, or derivative use requires a license. Contact [email protected] for licensing enquiries.",
